     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is typically 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, for 2,550 mg/day. This may be what you meant if 1700 was a typo.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another regimen**, such as a lower starting dose (500 mg once or twice daily) with titration.\n- **1700 mg three times daily, as written**. If this is deliberate, please confirm and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you verified the dose.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
